    "flyers: map-wide, one table per time of day (Morning/Afternoon/Evening/Night). The current time's table rolls every `interval` seconds with `chance`% to send a flock of ONE species from its `table` [{species, percent, scale, min, max, speed_min, speed_max, spin, erratic}] across the screen. scale = size multiplier (1 = normal). min/max = flock size; speed in px/s (the flock shares one); spin = turns as it flies, faster when faster; erratic = big jerky bat-like bob.",
